# Ctrl-C while a command runs. Each product's own shell tool and its own
# no-questions mode, so the command really starts: fx's `shell` under
# `yolo` ("full access"), xfx's `terminal` under `yolo`. The command sleeps
# six seconds; `cmd-done` is after it would have finished by itself.
fx: gateway interrupt-cmd-fx.json
xfx: gateway interrupt-cmd-xfx.json
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
# The full-access warning is up from the first frame for 4 s (capfile.py
# TIMERS): the turn starts once it has come and gone, so no snap below
# races it.
until shown Full access
wait 2
until gone Full access
type run cmd
key Enter
wait 2.5
snap cmd-running
key C-c
wait 0.4
snap cmd-cc
wait 1.5
snap cmd-cc-2
wait 4
# Ctrl-C's exit hint stays 3 s (capfile.py TIMERS): the snap below is the
# screen once it has gone, not a second count against it.
until gone press ctrl+c again to exit
snap cmd-done
snapfull end
gwlog
